  {
   "id": 324737,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Draw a Venn diagram to represent the relationship between each of the sets. All natural numbers are integers.\n\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The universal set is the set of integers. Draw a rectangle and label it with <span data-math=\"U = \\text{Integers}\">U = \\text{Integers}</span>. Next, draw a circle in the rectangle and label with Natural numbers.\n<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"https://exercises.openstax.org/rails/active_storage/blobs/proxy/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsibWVzc2FnZSI6IkJBaHBBcElPIiwiZXhwIjpudWxsLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--2c75ab942bd258c48e4497d6255d40da1eeb23f6/CS_Figure_01_03_010.png\" alt=\"A Venn diagram shows a circle placed inside a rectangle. The circle represents natural numbers and is shaded in yellow. The rectangle represents U equals integers and is shaded in blue.\">\n<figcaption>\nVenn diagram with universal set, <span data-math=\"U=\\text{Integers}\">U=\\text{Integers}</span>, and subset <span data-math=\"\\mathbb{N} = {\\text{Natural numbers}}\">\\mathbb{N} = {\\text{Natural numbers}}</span>.\n</figcaption>\n</figure>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 324738,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
